# Shared subagents that live in another git repository.
#
# One repository per line. Wagglebot clones it, takes the Markdown files at its
# top level, and installs each one as a subagent on every workstation. It writes
# every file to the location of each agent provider that supports subagents, so
# nobody needs to know where a provider stores its files.
#
# A repository on GitHub is written as owner/repo. Add @<tag-or-commit> to pin
# it. Pin every repository that the company does not control.
#   acme/review-agents@1a2b3c4
#
# A repository on any other git host is written as its full clone URL. Add a
# space and a tag or commit to pin it. The clone uses the git credentials of
# the workstation.
#   https://git.my-company.local/platform/agents.git v1.2.0
#   git@git.my-company.local:platform/agents.git
#
# Other kinds of subagent need no entry here:
#   - A subagent for the whole company is committed to company/agents/ in this repository.
#   - A subagent for one team is committed to teams/<team>/agents/.
#   - A subagent for one component is committed to .agents/subagents/ in the
#     repository of that component.
